From bd74d0d5a6251280d10c498d8f30a9f29c17bc82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tsetsen-erdene Ganbaatar <dis446@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:46:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app-core): harden project-defined tools after review

Reload project tools on every session attach, strip jcode's generic intent parameter, honour JCODE_HOME, and decouple project tools from MCP opt-outs. Bound the timeout around stdin, cap output while reading, and default global entries to the session cwd.

- Track project tools via Tool::is_project_tool and replace them on reload, so file edits and working-directory changes do not leave stale tools.
- Register project tools after the fixed MCP tools at every session site, so JCODE_RUN_MCP=0 and the no-MCP attach path still load them and mcp/mcp_search/mcp_call cannot be shadowed.
- Strip accept_large_output and intent (unless the schema declares intent) before writing stdin, matching the MCP tool path.
- Resolve the global file with storage::jcode_dir(), so JCODE_HOME sandboxes do not read the real user tools file.
- Load only the global file when no working dir is known; jcode run passes its process cwd explicitly.
- Default global entries to session cwd and repo entries to the repo root; resolve the global file's relative commands against the jcode home.
- Include stdin in the timeout and cap output without buffering it all.
- Add 19 project-tool tests, including reload, collision, intent, global cwd/base, JCODE_HOME, 128 KiB output cap and large-stdin timeout; gate execution tests to Unix.
- Update the project-tools documentation.
